## problems

1 - énorme overfitting
2 - mauvais split des données (des molécules de structure similaire sont dans le trainset et dans le valset donc aucune preuve de généralisation)
3 - score f1 très bas

## solutions

1 - régularisation:
    - increase dropout
    - switch optimizer to AdamW
    - increase weigth_decay

2 - find a way to split it well (with RDKit probably)

3 - set up all meta componnements:
    - early stopping callback (can be useless)
    - set up scheduler (reduceLrOnPlateau or cosinedecay)
    - dataside: use a (im)balanced dataset instead of a weighted sum
    - use focal loss (maybe later because advanced)

    - then:
        try some visualisation of the repartition of the predicted probabilities ouputed by the model to see its real performances

## protocol

each time a new solution is implemented, run a training and save it with a comment so we can asses what perfoms and why and track ours improvement
implements ONLY one at time so we can legitimatly ablate the working feature and keep it.
write down in `experiments.md` (or a shared gdoc) where each experiment is consigned with its tensorboard logs and its best checkpoint